# Button loading spinner

When a button triggers navigation, form submit, or any async/server work, show the moving circle spinner so users know processing is happening.

## Do
- Rely on the global `initButtonLoading()` behavior in `resources/js/app.js` for form submits and primary CTA links.
- Use existing classes: `btn-primary`, `btn-secondary`, `btn-ghost`, plus `btn-spinner` / `btn-loading` / `is-processing`.
- For custom async `type="button"` actions, add `data-loading-btn` or drive `btn-spinner` visibility from Alpine/state.

## Don't
- Put spinners on pure UI toggles (nav dropdowns, mobile menu, bag open, quote modal open).
- Opt out unless needed — only use `data-no-spinner` on controls that must never show loading.
